WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.334
Hey. can I get you guys anything
else before I close this check out?

2
00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.133
As a matter of
fact. you can.

3
00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.639
My partner.
Trapezius Milkington.

4
00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.572
would like to see something
in a Belgian waffle.

5
00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.109
Shawn. it's 12:30.

6
00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.805
I do not want waffles
or eggs or Malt-O-Meal.

7
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.610
All right. What would you recommend?

8
00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.846
Oh. my gosh! If you're going to
do this. I'm going to the bathroom.

9
00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.250
Excuse me.

10
00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.216
Don't mind him. His bladder's
probably smaller than yours.

11
00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:29.091
Now go ahead. and take my taste
buds on a fantastical journey.

12
00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:31.187
I don't know...
I like the burgers.

13
00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.789
Ah. ah. ah. I'm sorry.
I should have told you.

14
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:36.358
Only rule. it can't be something
that someone would order for lunch.

15
00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:38.529
Keep in mind. we want
to go off script here.

16
00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:42.632
Okay. I see. Well. in
that case I would recommend

17
00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:46.907
the pumpkin pancakes
with a side of lingcod.

18
00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.880
Does that work?
Let's get married.

19
00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:49.972
You don't even know me!

20
00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.280
Oh. really! Allow me
to introduce yourself.

21
00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.252
Jetta girl. maybe green.

22
00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:57.084
Backseat loaded with
empty Pinkberry cups.

23
00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.385
Oh. my God!

24
00:00:58.458 --> 00:01:01.518
Wrong! I drive a Jeep. A black Jeep.

25
00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.585
But you're dead-on
with the Pinkberry.

26
00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.358
So what do you think?
Should we set a date or what?

27
00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:07.263
Mmm. I'll think about it.

28
00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.130
Fair enough.
Mmm-hmm.

29
00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:12.995
Let me guess.

30
00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.901
She's considering your
proposal of marriage?

31
00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.237
How could you
possibly know that?

32
00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.005
Shawn. you use that
same tired-ass routine

33
00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.740
on every other waitress
that serves us.

34
00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.179
This is
categorically untrue.

35
00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:25.217
You used it on that 80-year-old
fixings attendant at Fuddruckers.

36
00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.981
What's your point. man? My point
is. you're going to be 80 years old

37
00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.954
and still shamelessly
hitting on waitresses.

38
00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.047
Is that what you want?

39
00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.148
Is that a trick question?

40
00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:33.624
What do you think?

41
00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:37.060
All right. Hitch. you want
me to take a chance? Huh?

42
00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:39.860
You want to see some
Will Hunting action?

43
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.358
Here we go.

44
00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.992
Who are you
calling? Juliet?

45
00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.094
That routine is as tired
as the waitress bit.

46
00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.195
Wait for it.

47
00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.736
<i>Wait for it.</i>

48
00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.738
Hello?

49
00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:00.513
Abigail Lytar?
Judd Nelson.

50
00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:02.987
Shawn. stop playing.
Is that really Abigail?

51
00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.417
Shawn. is that you?

52
00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.220
<i>Of course it is.
Don't be ridiculous.</i>

53
00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.988
Look. clearly. we left some loose
ends at our high school reunion.

54
00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:12.361
so I was thinking that
maybe we should get together.

55
00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.763
Why on earth would you
think that's a good idea?

56
00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:18.326
Oh. I don't know. the last time I saw
you. we kissed for like 27 seconds?

57
00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.395
Can I tell you something? Gord.

58
00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:26.007
So just us.
sitting at the same table?

59
00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:27.603
Hopefully a corner booth.

60
00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.843
Abigail. what's
happening here is.

61
00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:33.249
I'm asking you out
on a proper date.

62
00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.581
Shawn. are you sure?

63
00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.315
Are you sure about this?

64
00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.851
Yes. I believe I am.

65
00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.418
<i>Pick you up at 7:00.</i>

66
00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:43.761
I'll be the one flaring
my nostrils uncontrollably.

67
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:51.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

68
00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:00.303
Oh. God. no.

69
00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.218
Done. How do you like them apples?

70
00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.811
I sincerely hope you didn't
just do that to prove a point.

71
00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:11.015
She's a real person.
Shawn. That's no joke.

72
00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.183
She misses me
already.

73
00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.556
Oh. Chief!

74
00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:17.323
Get down here now.
I'm not asking.

75
00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:20.089
That's weird.

76
00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.895
We received the following letter about
an hour ago. It has been authenticated.

77
00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.665
It's from the Yin-Yang killer.

78
00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.763
Pay close attention.

79
00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.866
"Hey. everybody. I'm back.
for one night only.

80
00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:32.935
"I'm going to kill
someone tonight.

81
00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:35.003
"Guess who?
Guess where? Guess how?

82
00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.843
"This is going
to be so much fun.

83
00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.315
"Signed. Mr. Yang. "

84
00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.875
He's looking for a new
challenger. That's what he does.

85
00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:42.720
Chief. I believe
he's speaking to me.

86
00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.552
Trust me. I'm ready.

87
00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:55.095
Well. come on people. He
could be talking about anybody.

88
00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.465
Look. just last week.

89
00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:59.471
Officer Jankowicz guessed my
favorite variety of snack cracker.

90
00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.973
Tuscan wheat.
it's really obscure.

91
00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:15.854
<i>I know. you know
That I'm not telling the truth</i>

92
00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:18.789
<i>I know. you know
They just don't have any proof</i>

93
00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:22.225
<i>Embrace the deception
Learn how to bend</i>

94
00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:27.062
<i>Your worst inhibitions tend
to psych you out in the end</i>

95
00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.202
What do we have
on his description?

96
00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:40.542
We don't. We've never had any age.
ethnicity or physical description.

97
00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.877
The harsh truth
is that this is his game.

98
00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.610
And we just have
to play along with him.

99
00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:45.673
That's a terrific plan.

100
00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:48.277
Especially since it's worked
out so well in the past.

101
00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.719
Chief. the Mayor's
on the phone.

102
00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.689
Oh. here we go.
Detective Lassiter.

103
00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:53.658
introduce Shawn
to our point person.

104
00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.421
Spencer. listen up.
Whoa. whoa. whoa.

105
00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:57.087
Getting... I'm getting
something already.

106
00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:59.097
What? What is it?
I can see the killer.

107
00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:00.928
Already?
Yes.

108
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.592
And I know exactly
where he is.

109
00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.503
Right there.
Come on. that's our guy.

110
00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.665
Shawn.

111
00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.504
Shawn. that is
Mary Lightly.

112
00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:13.568
our profiler from the Serial
Homicide and Abduction Task Force.

113
00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.773
He is very familiar with
the patterns of our killer.

114
00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:18.112
And how to make an attractive
lamp out of human skin.

115
00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:21.017
Shawn. play nice. He's a
genius. and we need him.

116
00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:23.949
Mary. this is...

117
00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:26.514
Shawn Spencer.
in the flesh.

118
00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:27.650
See? He said "flesh. "

119
00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:31.187
You know him? I've
done my research. okay?

120
00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:32.856
Yeah. well.
I've Googled myself. too.

121
00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.763
and there's a lot
of stuff missing.

122
00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:37.325
This is my partner.
Sterling Cooper.

123
00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.101
Hello.

124
00:05:46.446 --> 00:05:47.936
So what's "Mary"
short for? Marion?

125
00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.481
No.

126
00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:50.538
Great.
we're all good friends.

127
00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:53.050
Care to shed a little
light on this subject?

128
00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:57.351
Mr. Yang is the most notorious
killer this city has never seen.

129
00:05:57.423 --> 00:06:00.324
He claimed six victims
in the summer of 1995.

130
00:06:00.393 --> 00:06:03.294
and has resurfaced twice. claiming
a single victim in each instance.

131
00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:06.230
He only resurfaces when he
feels there's a worthy opponent.

132
00:06:06.299 --> 00:06:08.290
Now. his M.O.
Is to challenge us

133
00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:12.270
with the opportunity to save the
victims by solving his riddles.

134
00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:14.499
Question. regarding
the whole Mary thing.

135
00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:15.563
My father's name
was Mary.

136
00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:17.131
His father before him
was named Mary.

137
00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.678
and his father before him
was named Craig.

138
00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:21.236
Fair enough. Proceed.

139
00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:22.576
Yin-Yang.

140
00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:26.515
The origin of this Chinese
symbol is the unity of opposites.

141
00:06:26.586 --> 00:06:29.578
Two opposing. and at the same
time. complimentary aspects.

142
00:06:29.655 --> 00:06:33.523
Dark versus light. Killer
versus cop. Kramer versus Kramer.

143
00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:34.992
Just show him the riddle.

144
00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:37.659
"She serves the General
well today

145
00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.425
"whose soldiers
wait to die.

146
00:06:39.499 --> 00:06:41.399
"In a white river
they shall pay

147
00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:44.334
"for them she will not cry. Who is she?"

148
00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:48.067
Now. this riddle came with
this stopwatch already running.

149
00:06:48.141 --> 00:06:49.972
One of his classic moves.

150
00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:52.510
We've got one hour
and ten minutes. people.

151
00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.978
Generals and soldiers. She'd
be in the military. McNab!

152
00:06:55.047 --> 00:06:56.639
Yes. sir!
Damn it.

153
00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:58.843
I want you to contact every
military base in an 80-mile radius.

154
00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.443
Find out if any female personnel
have gone AWOL in the last 48 hours.

155
00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:04.915
And bear in mind. it's the
psychic that he wants to play with.

156
00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:07.425
Each riddle will relate
to him. personally.

157
00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.052
Do you have
any thoughts. Shawn?

158
00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:11.892
Yes. Jules. I do.

159
00:07:11.998 --> 00:07:15.456
First of all. his rhyming
skills are rudimentary at best.

160
00:07:15.535 --> 00:07:18.504
"Today" and "pay"? "Die" and
"cry"? Come on. That's bush league.

161
00:07:18.805 --> 00:07:20.067
It's
bush. Lassy!

162
00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:21.936
Spencer. stop screwing
around. Get on with it.

163
00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:24.602
I understand.
Yes. Thank you. sir.

164
00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:27.111
Karen. you're not going
to use my son as a pawn.

165
00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:29.148
Oh. I'll advise you
to proceed with caution.

166
00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:30.307
Need I remind you
what happened

167
00:07:30.383 --> 00:07:32.908
to the last detective who went
head-to-head with this sick bastard?

168
00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:35.044
He lost. and
an innocent girl died.

169
00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:37.851
Now. I will thank you to go
home and let us do our work!

170
00:07:37.924 --> 00:07:39.084
Not going to happen.

171
00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:40.591
Not going to happen!
Henry!

172
00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:43.985
Your son is the only shot
that we have. Period.

173
00:07:44.864 --> 00:07:46.957
Yeah. well.
not my problem.

174
00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:50.627
Thus far...
Shawn!

175
00:07:52.338 --> 00:07:53.703
Excuse me.

176
00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:57.331
Hey. did I miss
a memo?

177
00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.934
I thought Bring Your Daddy
to Work Day was next week.

178
00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:01.479
I forbid you to be a part of
this. Shawn. You're coming with me.

179
00:08:01.547 --> 00:08:03.208
Whoa. whoa. whoa. whoa.
Forbid me?

180
00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:05.113
I'm familiar with your
hands-on approach to parenting.

181
00:08:05.184 --> 00:08:07.175
but I'm not 27 anymore.
I can do whatever I want.

182
00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:08.379
This guy
knows about you.

183
00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:10.615
he knows about
everybody you care about.

184
00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:11.714
Think about that.

185
00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:13.486
You don't catch this
son of a bitch. kid.

186
00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:14.651
you're never going
to sleep again.

187
00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:17.491
Spencer. 55 minutes.

188
00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:23.794
Go home. Dad.
I've got this.

189
00:08:25.037 --> 00:08:26.265
Go home.

190
00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:32.406
<i>Sorry. guys. My dad was just
dropping off my Zodiac DVD.</i>

191
00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:34.275
Can we focus. please?

192
00:08:35.181 --> 00:08:36.648
"In a white river
they shall pay. "

193
00:08:36.716 --> 00:08:38.047
His seventh victim
washed up on shore.

194
00:08:38.117 --> 00:08:40.517
Maybe there's a... No! There's
never a repeat performance.

195
00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:42.816
Okay? Each victim
is a new masterpiece.

196
00:08:42.889 --> 00:08:45.119
and the first riddle
is always a gimme.

197
00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:46.522
This guy is itching
to play the game.

198
00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:48.082
Think about
the last 24 hours.

199
00:08:49.195 --> 00:08:51.686
Gus! Gus. I got it. I mean.
I know who the General is.

200
00:08:51.764 --> 00:08:52.992
His name is Mills.

201
00:08:53.065 --> 00:08:54.930
General Mills.
the cereal manufacturer?

202
00:08:55.001 --> 00:08:58.835
Exactly! The white river is
milk. and the soldiers are cereal.

203
00:08:58.905 --> 00:09:00.395
So who is she?

204
00:09:08.848 --> 00:09:10.975
Hi. welcome to Captain
Ron's. Table for five?

205
00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.780
There was a waitress here
earlier. long brown hair.

206
00:09:13.853 --> 00:09:15.548
I haven't seen her in a
while. She must be on break.

207
00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:17.612
Where? In the back. by the lockers.

208
00:09:24.764 --> 00:09:25.753
How do you know
this girl?

209
00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:26.991
We don't really know her.

210
00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:29.495
She served us
our lunch.

211
00:09:47.353 --> 00:09:51.585
"Oh. rats. Shawn. so close.
Too bad she has to die.

212
00:09:51.657 --> 00:09:56.185
"But how? And when? And where?
Don't bother asking why. "

213
00:09:57.263 --> 00:09:59.163
Well. he still
owes us a riddle.

214
00:09:59.231 --> 00:10:02.496
<i>This is just the amuse-bouche.
He's taunting you.</i>

215
00:10:02.568 --> 00:10:05.036
I believe he's using the
Alpha-Bits to send a message.

216
00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:09.131
that he. too. believes that
breakfast for lunch is way underrated.

217
00:10:09.208 --> 00:10:11.506
Would anyone like to try writing
this message with a burrito?

218
00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:13.476
Open challenge.
Take a shot.

219
00:10:13.546 --> 00:10:15.343
Exactly.
I rest my case.

220
00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:17.143
And now
I want a burrito.

221
00:10:17.216 --> 00:10:19.377
Can I talk to you
for a second. please?

222
00:10:19.452 --> 00:10:21.511
Dude. what are you doing?
What are you talking about?

223
00:10:21.587 --> 00:10:23.487
A girl's life is at stake
and you're acting like an ass?

224
00:10:23.556 --> 00:10:24.580
Making jokes?

225
00:10:24.657 --> 00:10:26.557
You haven't taken this thing
seriously from jump street.

226
00:10:26.626 --> 00:10:27.820
Exactly.
Exactly?

227
00:10:27.893 --> 00:10:30.123
Gus. I have to work
like this. okay?

228
00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:31.356
That guy gets
in my head. we lose.

229
00:10:32.164 --> 00:10:34.359
I have to do my thing.
I cannot show weakness.

230
00:10:34.433 --> 00:10:36.697
And my fanciful rhetoric
helps defuse a situation

231
00:10:36.769 --> 00:10:37.793
that's very tense
for the group.

232
00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:39.497
But Shawn.
nobody is laughing.

233
00:10:39.572 --> 00:10:41.767
Trust me. They're
laughing on the inside.

234
00:10:41.841 --> 00:10:43.240
That's how
it works. buddy.

235
00:10:43.309 --> 00:10:44.867
And I need you
to help me out here.

236
00:10:44.944 --> 00:10:46.639
Do you think
you can do that?

237
00:10:46.712 --> 00:10:48.441
I'll try.
All right.

238
00:10:50.149 --> 00:10:52.743
"Little League is over.
You just became a pro.

239
00:10:52.818 --> 00:10:54.718
"Score a run.
we'll have more fun.

240
00:10:54.787 --> 00:10:56.220
"Make sure you
beat the throw. "

241
00:10:56.589 --> 00:10:58.614
Next location.
How much time do we have?

242
00:10:59.291 --> 00:11:00.280
Seventeen minutes.

243
00:11:00.359 --> 00:11:01.792
Wow.

244
00:11:02.428 --> 00:11:04.828
I want pancakes.
Who wants some pancakes?

245
00:11:04.897 --> 00:11:07.297
Whipped butter.
Maple syrup. What?

246
00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:13.000
"Make sure you beat the throw"
insinuates a close play.

247
00:11:14.006 --> 00:11:15.405
You gotta touch
home plate.

248
00:11:15.474 --> 00:11:17.101
You gotta touch home
plate to score a run.

249
00:11:17.176 --> 00:11:18.768
That means the clue is back
at the police station.

250
00:11:19.912 --> 00:11:21.402
Hmm. Mmm-hmm.

251
00:11:22.948 --> 00:11:24.745
Make a hole!

252
00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:28.077
Mom?
Hey. goose.

253
00:11:30.222 --> 00:11:31.553
Hi. Mrs. Spencer.
Hey.

254
00:11:31.624 --> 00:11:32.989
Spencer! Let's go!

255
00:11:33.826 --> 00:11:35.157
We need to talk.
I'll make it quick.

256
00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:37.593
Sure. no problem. Find the
clue. I'll be right there!

257
00:11:37.663 --> 00:11:38.857
Bye.
Bye

258
00:11:39.398 --> 00:11:40.660
I'm not going
to mince words.

259
00:11:40.733 --> 00:11:42.826
Your father called me.
he's worried about you.

260
00:11:42.902 --> 00:11:44.927
He wants me to convince
you not to do this.

261
00:11:45.004 --> 00:11:47.268
So he calls you. you hop on a
plane. That's how it works. huh?

262
00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:48.829
No. Shawn. I didn't
fly down here.

263
00:11:48.908 --> 00:11:50.398
I was at a conference
in Ventura.

264
00:11:50.476 --> 00:11:52.944
You were in town?
Would've been nice to know.

265
00:11:53.012 --> 00:11:55.879
Truth is. I'm worried
about you. too.

266
00:11:55.948 --> 00:11:57.643
I did psych evals
of several officers

267
00:11:57.717 --> 00:12:00.242
who were involved in this first
round of this maniac's game.

268
00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:01.684
It wasn't pretty.

269
00:12:01.754 --> 00:12:03.153
All right. look.

270
00:12:03.222 --> 00:12:06.487
first of all. Mom. I have
a date tonight. All right?

271
00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:08.117
So I have to wrap this up
at a reasonable hour.

272
00:12:08.194 --> 00:12:12.358
And secondly. this guy has
never gone up against me.

273
00:12:12.431 --> 00:12:14.695
If I can stand here. and tell
you that I will nail this guy.

274
00:12:14.767 --> 00:12:17.133
are you really going
to tell me to walk away?

275
00:12:17.203 --> 00:12:18.534
Shawn!
Mom!

276
00:12:19.171 --> 00:12:20.695
I can beat him.

277
00:12:21.774 --> 00:12:22.763
I will

278
00:12:23.242 --> 00:12:24.231
beat him.

279
00:12:27.847 --> 00:12:29.974
Okay. goose. Nail
the son of a bitch.

280
00:12:30.049 --> 00:12:32.347
Yeah. Okay.
I've got to go. Mom.

281
00:12:36.088 --> 00:12:37.316
Please be right.

282
00:12:37.823 --> 00:12:39.848
Spencer! Conference room. Thanks.

283
00:12:40.292 --> 00:12:42.226
Well. someone must
have signed for this.

284
00:12:42.294 --> 00:12:44.421
It wasn't delivered. Dobson
found it outside the file room.

285
00:12:44.497 --> 00:12:45.964
Well. how
in the hell can...

286
00:12:46.999 --> 00:12:49.559
Okay. you know what.
people? Eyes open!

287
00:12:49.635 --> 00:12:51.569
<i>Chief? Lou Sardocki from the
Independent is on the phone.</i>

288
00:12:51.637 --> 00:12:52.626
He says you owe him
a statement?

289
00:12:52.705 --> 00:12:55.139
Oh. I'll give him a statement.

290
00:13:06.519 --> 00:13:07.747
That's pretty clever.

291
00:13:11.957 --> 00:13:13.982
"Meet my little
buddy Ben. "

292
00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:19.998
"Pitter patter is your hint. If you can't
remember when. just read the fine print. "

293
00:13:23.536 --> 00:13:25.731
And we have
less than one hour.

294
00:13:25.805 --> 00:13:28.968
Shawn. can you
speak to it?

295
00:13:29.041 --> 00:13:30.668
No. he can't
speak to it!

296
00:13:30.743 --> 00:13:33.371
Yes. he can. Just give
him some room. Back up.

297
00:13:33.445 --> 00:13:35.072
Fine. knock yourself
out. Doctor Dolittle.

298
00:13:35.147 --> 00:13:37.741
"Doctor Dolittle"? I know you
can do better than that. Lassy.

299
00:13:37.817 --> 00:13:39.011
I know you can.

300
00:13:43.789 --> 00:13:46.155
I don't... I don't know what
I'm supposed to remember.

301
00:13:49.628 --> 00:13:51.789
Hey. everybody.
Guess who I am?

302
00:13:51.864 --> 00:13:52.888
<i>Hee. hee</i>

303
00:14:00.439 --> 00:14:02.202
I'm Michael Jackson.

304
00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:04.141
King of pop.

305
00:14:08.914 --> 00:14:11.474
Shawn. I don't think this is working.

306
00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:15.213
Are you kidding me? That was a
home run. Keep up the good work.

307
00:14:15.287 --> 00:14:17.448
"Pitter patter"
is the hint.

308
00:14:17.523 --> 00:14:20.492
Now. I don't think
we're speaking to a mouse.

309
00:14:20.559 --> 00:14:22.220
I think the mouse
is speaking to you.

310
00:14:23.128 --> 00:14:25.062
What do you got. Shawn?

311
00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.529
"Fine print. "

312
00:14:28.701 --> 00:14:29.725
Hello. my friend.

313
00:14:31.704 --> 00:14:33.797
It's the fine print.
He was walking on it.

314
00:14:36.308 --> 00:14:37.639
Dude. this is crazy!

315
00:14:38.244 --> 00:14:41.771
"Adam Hornstock selling
black snake. Will go fast. "

316
00:14:41.847 --> 00:14:46.045
"Mira Gaffney seeks Bruton
Gaster to love her tender. "

317
00:14:46.118 --> 00:14:48.143
All people
from past cases.

318
00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:49.346
How do you know that?

319
00:14:49.421 --> 00:14:50.683
I told you.
I did my research.

320
00:14:50.756 --> 00:14:53.520
And finding Bouchard's treasure
was extremely impressive.

321
00:14:53.592 --> 00:14:54.581
Thank you. Willard.

322
00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.127
My pleasure.

323
00:14:56.195 --> 00:15:01.929
"Snarky psychic seeks ferroequinologist
to help with killer smile. "

324
00:15:03.269 --> 00:15:04.668
He's calling me snarky?

325
00:15:04.737 --> 00:15:06.136
"Ferroequinologist"?

326
00:15:06.205 --> 00:15:08.696
A ferroequinologist
is a train enthusiast.

327
00:15:08.774 --> 00:15:09.832
How do you know that?

328
00:15:09.909 --> 00:15:11.740
Because I am
a ferroequinologist.

329
00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:13.402
I too. am
a ferroequinologist.

330
00:15:13.479 --> 00:15:14.878
"Love her tender. "

331
00:15:14.947 --> 00:15:17.415
The tender is a small fuel car
right behind the locomotive.

332
00:15:17.883 --> 00:15:20.511
And "black snake"
is slang for coal train.

333
00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:22.577
There's only one coal train
that runs through Santa Barbara.

334
00:15:23.722 --> 00:15:24.711
Thank God.

335
00:15:30.262 --> 00:15:32.958
The train's right on
time. That is outstanding.

336
00:15:33.032 --> 00:15:34.431
It's not
going to stop.

337
00:15:35.301 --> 00:15:36.290
What?

338
00:15:36.368 --> 00:15:37.494
It's not
going to stop.

339
00:15:37.569 --> 00:15:39.196
This is just
a pull-through station.

340
00:15:39.271 --> 00:15:40.795
What the hell
are we doing here?

341
00:15:45.878 --> 00:15:47.209
Come on!
What the...

342
00:15:49.581 --> 00:15:50.673
Where the hell
are you going?

343
00:15:50.983 --> 00:15:54.180
Come on. Gus. This is our fantasy.
man! It's like we're hobos.

344
00:15:54.253 --> 00:15:56.687
I don't have
a hobo fantasy. Shawn.

345
00:15:59.325 --> 00:16:00.690
Abigail. you
called me back!

346
00:16:00.759 --> 00:16:04.661
Yes. you left me very specific
instructions in your message to do so.

347
00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.595
<i>Is this a bad time?
No. I can talk!</i>

348
00:16:06.665 --> 00:16:08.360
Look. we're still
totally on for tonight.

349
00:16:08.434 --> 00:16:10.334
I might just have to push
the time a little bit.

350
00:16:10.402 --> 00:16:14.702
Uh-huh. Let me guess. you're
chasing a serial killer or something.

351
00:16:15.207 --> 00:16:19.041
Holy crap. yes! Yes. that's
exactly what I'm doing! How did...

352
00:16:19.111 --> 00:16:21.705
I cannot believe that you are
bailing on me again!

353
00:16:21.914 --> 00:16:23.006
Hold on!

354
00:16:23.449 --> 00:16:24.814
Tell Abigail
what we're doing!

355
00:16:27.953 --> 00:16:29.944
Hello. Abigail!
It's Gus!

356
00:16:30.923 --> 00:16:32.720
We're chasing
a train like hobos!

357
00:16:34.193 --> 00:16:35.285
What?

358
00:16:37.062 --> 00:16:39.155
She wants
to talk with you.

359
00:16:39.698 --> 00:16:41.928
First of all. his
out-of-breath voice is terrible.

360
00:16:42.001 --> 00:16:44.561
<i>He was bad in Othello
senior year. he's bad now.</i>

361
00:16:44.636 --> 00:16:46.729
Look. I'm just flashing
back to high school.

362
00:16:46.805 --> 00:16:50.036
and I have this image of me standing
alone on a pier looking like an idiot.

363
00:16:50.342 --> 00:16:52.037
Look. I swear I'm
telling the truth!

364
00:16:52.544 --> 00:16:53.738
I'm going to have
to call you back!

365
00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.407
By the way. you were
beautiful on that pier!

366
00:17:15.801 --> 00:17:16.859
Ah!

367
00:17:18.137 --> 00:17:20.196
"A moving picture
is worth a thousand words.

368
00:17:20.305 --> 00:17:23.001
"so read the story
and follow the birds.

369
00:17:23.075 --> 00:17:25.305
"P.S. Once you're there
you'll hear a phone.

370
00:17:25.377 --> 00:17:26.969
"You have eight rings
to pick up.

371
00:17:27.246 --> 00:17:28.508
"or the girl is dead.

372
00:17:29.548 --> 00:17:31.516
"Shame on me.
that didn't even rhyme. "

373
00:17:32.684 --> 00:17:34.584
We have 27 minutes
to solve this.

374
00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:41.526
Okay. Here. This is. uh...
Okay...

375
00:17:42.861 --> 00:17:43.953
What do you see?

376
00:17:44.029 --> 00:17:46.691
Nothing. I don't see
anything. Not yet.

377
00:17:50.002 --> 00:17:52.027
Oh. wait. I do see
something. What? What is it?

378
00:17:52.104 --> 00:17:53.799
I think you're going to want
to see this. It's pretty good.

379
00:17:56.008 --> 00:17:57.134
Let me on.

380
00:18:03.148 --> 00:18:04.809
Mary. I'm surprised
it took you so long.

381
00:18:04.883 --> 00:18:06.145
You seemed to spry.

382
00:18:06.218 --> 00:18:07.378
Ankle weights.

383
00:18:09.421 --> 00:18:10.854
I always wear them.
Even when I sleep.

384
00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.387
<i>I read about it
in Men's Fitness.</i>

385
00:18:14.359 --> 00:18:16.190
Totally reinvigorated
Ryan Reynolds' career.

386
00:18:18.063 --> 00:18:19.428
So what's the riddle?
How can I help?

387
00:18:20.299 --> 00:18:21.823
"A moving...
A moving picture.

388
00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:24.164
"A moving picture
is worth a thousand words. "

389
00:18:44.656 --> 00:18:47.056
You've got to be kidding me.
You've got to be kidding me!

390
00:18:47.126 --> 00:18:49.959
I got it!
I solved it! Let's go!

391
00:18:57.302 --> 00:18:59.327
That's it! That's it!
That's it! That's it!

392
00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:06.637
"Follow the birds. "

393
00:19:30.202 --> 00:19:31.362
There.

394
00:19:37.643 --> 00:19:39.338
That's five rings.
Shawn! Answer it!

395
00:19:40.679 --> 00:19:41.771
Shawn. what
are you doing?

396
00:19:41.847 --> 00:19:44.407
No. don't you see? It didn't start
ringing until we were three feet away.

397
00:19:44.483 --> 00:19:45.643
Answer the phone.
Spencer!

398
00:19:45.717 --> 00:19:47.912
He's watching us
right now from somewhere!

399
00:19:47.986 --> 00:19:49.317
Answer the phone. Shawn!

400
00:19:59.464 --> 00:20:02.092
If that girl dies. you're
an accessory to murder.

401
00:20:10.309 --> 00:20:12.368
Shawn. I hope to God
you know what you're doing.

402
00:20:19.651 --> 00:20:20.743
Unbelievable.

403
00:20:45.277 --> 00:20:46.369
He's been here.

404
00:20:46.445 --> 00:20:48.606
He was here watching us
the whole time!

405
00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:49.977
Don't touch anything.

406
00:20:50.048 --> 00:20:51.845
Let's get CSI down here
to dust for prints.

407
00:20:51.917 --> 00:20:54.647
There's no need.
I'm sure he touched things.

408
00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:55.744
He probably touched
everything.

409
00:20:55.821 --> 00:20:58.881
but you're not going to find any
prints. He's too good for that.

410
00:20:58.957 --> 00:21:02.290
What is this sick. twisted admiration
you have for this whack job?

411
00:21:02.361 --> 00:21:04.090
Now do you get
how good he is?

412
00:21:04.162 --> 00:21:05.288
This puppy's
just warming up.

413
00:21:12.471 --> 00:21:13.733
Hey everybody. check it out.

414
00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:17.436
Look how big I am
compared to this plane.

415
00:21:23.448 --> 00:21:24.972
I'm King Kong.

416
00:21:25.917 --> 00:21:27.578
Guster. what the hell
is going on with you?

417
00:21:27.653 --> 00:21:30.281
Seriously. man. I need you
to pull yourself together.

418
00:21:40.565 --> 00:21:41.930
Oh. my God.

419
00:21:43.335 --> 00:21:44.734
Let me see that.

420
00:21:58.183 --> 00:21:59.445
I got it!

421
00:22:01.353 --> 00:22:03.014
It's a message.

422
00:22:03.088 --> 00:22:05.818
He says. "You are a
naughty. naughty boy. "

423
00:22:06.625 --> 00:22:08.616
He's giving us another
chance. She's still alive.

424
00:22:08.694 --> 00:22:10.355
Let's go back to the station.
wait for instructions.

425
00:22:10.429 --> 00:22:11.794
Forget that.
I'm... I'm not going.

426
00:22:11.863 --> 00:22:14.627
What do you mean?
I'm nobody's puppet. okay?

427
00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:16.565
I'm done. I'm done
playing his little game.

428
00:22:16.635 --> 00:22:19.570
I solved his puzzles. I talked
to a rat. I even chased a train.

429
00:22:19.638 --> 00:22:20.627
I'm finished.

430
00:22:20.706 --> 00:22:22.731
No one's ever gotten this far.
That's why he's still playing.

431
00:22:22.808 --> 00:22:23.797
It's a sign of respect.

432
00:22:23.875 --> 00:22:26.810
No. It isn't. Mary.
You said it. man.

433
00:22:26.878 --> 00:22:28.812
with your fey name and
your weird Ken Burns haircut.

434
00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:30.177
He's too good!

435
00:22:30.248 --> 00:22:32.478
Isn't that right?
He's better than me!

436
00:22:32.551 --> 00:22:35.315
We never had a chance! He's going
to kill that girl either way!

437
00:22:35.387 --> 00:22:38.117
Maybe. maybe not. Shawn. but I
know this. you don't just give up.

438
00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:42.889
Tell you what. Jules. uh. the next time
a serial killer calls you out. personally.

439
00:22:42.961 --> 00:22:44.588
you can pick up
your little pompoms

440
00:22:44.663 --> 00:22:46.631
and you can rally the troops
and never say die.

441
00:22:46.698 --> 00:22:47.960
I'm out.

442
00:22:48.567 --> 00:22:51.001
Now. get out.
All three of you.

443
00:22:51.069 --> 00:22:52.195
I can't believe
I'm hearing this.

444
00:22:52.270 --> 00:22:53.259
Should I
say it again?

445
00:22:53.338 --> 00:22:56.398
You know what? Screw you.
Spencer. We don't need you!

446
00:22:56.475 --> 00:22:58.875
We don't need him. O'Hara. We
will find this sicko on our own.

447
00:22:58.944 --> 00:23:00.639
Come on!
We're running out of time.

448
00:23:12.624 --> 00:23:15.787
Look. Shawn. I know you're
upset. but if we give up now...

449
00:23:15.861 --> 00:23:18.125
<i>Gus. don't be The Last of the
Famous International Playboys.</i>

450
00:23:18.196 --> 00:23:19.754
We're not giving up. okay?
Far from it.

451
00:23:19.831 --> 00:23:21.628
The only chance we have
to win the game at this point

452
00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:22.997
is to change
the rules. okay?

453
00:23:23.068 --> 00:23:25.832
I took a risk out there because
I knew he wouldn't kill her.

454
00:23:25.904 --> 00:23:27.997
I knew he wouldn't kill her
because he loves the game too much.

455
00:23:28.073 --> 00:23:30.974
but that bought us time. It bought
us time to work by ourselves.

456
00:23:31.042 --> 00:23:33.772
Okay? We're going to... We're
going to drop off his radar.

457
00:23:33.845 --> 00:23:34.869
We're still going
to find the girl.

458
00:23:34.946 --> 00:23:36.811
We're going to do it
on our own. That's our move.

459
00:23:36.882 --> 00:23:38.873
All right.
but where do we start?

460
00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:40.144
We go back
to the beginning.

461
00:23:40.218 --> 00:23:43.153
Back to the beginning. and we
trace the steps of Mr. Yang.

462
00:23:44.055 --> 00:23:46.216
All right. You like what
I did with the King Kong?

463
00:23:46.291 --> 00:23:48.191
You're on fire.
You're even using props.

464
00:23:48.260 --> 00:23:51.195
Just got this fax. Traced
it to a bogus 800 number.

465
00:23:51.263 --> 00:23:53.697
"I'm no Doubting Thomas.
I pucker up to fights.

466
00:23:53.765 --> 00:23:57.428
"Were you to shake my hand. you'd
have to use your right. Who am I?"

467
00:23:57.502 --> 00:23:59.936
Well. if Yang was watching. he
couldn't know if Spencer flew the coop.

468
00:24:00.005 --> 00:24:01.973
This could be directed
at any one of us.

469
00:24:02.908 --> 00:24:04.341
Probably not
this guy.

470
00:24:04.409 --> 00:24:07.037
It's me.
It's directed at me.

471
00:24:07.112 --> 00:24:08.704
He must know
I'm a Civil War buff.

472
00:24:08.780 --> 00:24:11.874
1863. Confederate General
Thomas "Stonewall" Jackson

473
00:24:11.950 --> 00:24:14.510
was shot and killed by his own troops
at the Battle of Chancellorsville.

474
00:24:14.586 --> 00:24:17.487
He was known for sucking on
lemons. even during combat.

475
00:24:17.556 --> 00:24:19.319
And while he is buried
in Lexington. Virginia.

476
00:24:19.391 --> 00:24:21.655
his left arm is buried
separately near the battlefield.

477
00:24:21.726 --> 00:24:24.991
<i>Hey. you guys remember that Pat
Swayze miniseries. North and South?</i>

478
00:24:25.063 --> 00:24:26.587
Talk about
Civil War buff. huh?

479
00:24:27.699 --> 00:24:28.688
Oh. my God!

480
00:24:28.767 --> 00:24:32.259
The Stonewall Hotel and
Suites! Probably room 1863!

481
00:24:32.337 --> 00:24:33.361
We've got to get
down there.

482
00:24:33.438 --> 00:24:35.565
And you can count me in for
next year's reenactment. partner.

483
00:24:35.640 --> 00:24:37.130
Copy that.
Get my jacket.

484
00:24:38.944 --> 00:24:40.673
Look. call me back. okay?
We're still on for tonight.

485
00:24:40.745 --> 00:24:43.213
Gus and I are making some
serious progress here.

486
00:24:43.281 --> 00:24:44.441
Call me back!

487
00:24:44.749 --> 00:24:46.080
Straight to voicemail.
That's not a good sign.

488
00:24:49.855 --> 00:24:52.346
Wrong! I drive a Jeep. A black Jeep.

489
00:24:53.291 --> 00:24:56.260
Gus. there's no Jeep. I think
he drove away in her car.

490
00:24:56.328 --> 00:24:58.728
We find the car.
we may find the girl.

491
00:24:59.664 --> 00:25:01.063
Lassiter. hold on.

492
00:25:02.934 --> 00:25:04.731
Find the girl's car.
It's a black Jeep.

493
00:25:04.903 --> 00:25:06.530
We already did.
You got to get down here.

494
00:25:06.605 --> 00:25:07.697
Where are you?

495
00:25:12.811 --> 00:25:14.005
SBPD!

496
00:25:14.579 --> 00:25:15.568
Room's clear!

497
00:25:16.681 --> 00:25:18.171
Clear!

498
00:25:22.354 --> 00:25:24.117
She's breathing.
I'll get the paramedics.

499
00:25:25.423 --> 00:25:26.890
What is this?

500
00:25:28.593 --> 00:25:30.993
"Shawn no longer
wants to play.

501
00:25:31.062 --> 00:25:33.462
"Stakes too low
to make you stay"?

502
00:25:49.281 --> 00:25:52.341
He's... He's got her. Gus.

503
00:25:58.223 --> 00:25:59.815
He's got my mom.

504
00:26:10.735 --> 00:26:12.566
Okay. I sent
a couple of officers

505
00:26:12.637 --> 00:26:15.401
over to Abigail Lytar's
apartment. and she's fine.

506
00:26:15.473 --> 00:26:18.772
But I'm posting them on a watch until
we can figure out what is going on.

507
00:26:18.843 --> 00:26:20.333
Spencer.
you need to get in here.

508
00:26:26.451 --> 00:26:29.215
"You should be moving.
as most people do.

509
00:26:29.287 --> 00:26:31.881
"but instead you sit
and enjoy the view.

510
00:26:31.957 --> 00:26:34.016
"P.S. Mommy says. 'Hi'

511
00:26:34.426 --> 00:26:37.156
and 'Bye'.
Just in case. "

512
00:26:37.629 --> 00:26:40.325
"VU." Why did he
spell it that way?

513
00:26:40.398 --> 00:26:41.695
Maybe that's the hint.

514
00:26:42.300 --> 00:26:44.063
Or maybe he
ran out of lipstick.

515
00:26:44.202 --> 00:26:45.294
Brendan Vu.

516
00:26:51.109 --> 00:26:52.633
From the spelling bee.

517
00:26:52.711 --> 00:26:55.236
Good guess.
but it's a misdirect.

518
00:26:55.981 --> 00:26:57.573
I know exactly what
he wants me to watch.

519
00:26:58.049 --> 00:26:59.243
You do?

520
00:27:08.093 --> 00:27:09.924
This is like
a needle in a haystack

521
00:27:09.995 --> 00:27:11.622
made completely
out of needles.

522
00:27:11.696 --> 00:27:13.357
Looks like we're
at the end game.

523
00:27:13.431 --> 00:27:16.059
All right. we know he used the waitress's
car. so there's a good chance...

524
00:27:16.134 --> 00:27:18.102
It's definitely a chance. What
kind of car does your wife drive?

525
00:27:18.169 --> 00:27:19.466
She rents when
she's down here.

526
00:27:19.537 --> 00:27:20.731
Do you know what company she rents from?

527
00:27:20.805 --> 00:27:22.136
That could narrow it
down to a few models.

528
00:27:26.778 --> 00:27:28.177
It's blue.

529
00:27:28.246 --> 00:27:30.544
It's blue. Gus. We're looking
for a blue car. It's a sedan.

530
00:27:30.915 --> 00:27:33.042
People. we're looking for a
blue car! A sedan! Go. go. go!

531
00:27:33.118 --> 00:27:34.779
All right. split up.
Squad. cover the exits!

532
00:27:35.253 --> 00:27:37.187
West side! West side!
Roger that.

533
00:27:42.961 --> 00:27:45.122
Hey. man! Watch
where you're going!

534
00:27:47.632 --> 00:27:49.998
Hey! Get off!

535
00:27:50.502 --> 00:27:51.594
Get off the car!

536
00:28:00.311 --> 00:28:01.437
Get off my car. man!

537
00:28:13.725 --> 00:28:15.124
Hey. Ma.

538
00:28:21.833 --> 00:28:24.734
Shawn! Shawn! Shh. shh!
Dad. get down. get down.

539
00:28:32.410 --> 00:28:33.399
Oh. jeez.

540
00:28:47.092 --> 00:28:48.582
Mom.

541
00:28:50.061 --> 00:28:51.858
I'm going to take
this off. okay?

542
00:28:51.930 --> 00:28:53.989
Mmm.
It's okay.

543
00:28:54.065 --> 00:28:55.191
It's just a decoy.

544
00:28:55.266 --> 00:28:56.699
I know. I see that.

545
00:29:05.577 --> 00:29:07.841
He's fine. He's breathing.
Yang must have knocked him out.

546
00:29:07.912 --> 00:29:09.004
SWAT. call for a medic!

547
00:29:09.080 --> 00:29:10.240
Yes. ma'am.

548
00:29:19.824 --> 00:29:21.189
Oh. my God.

549
00:29:25.263 --> 00:29:26.423
Dad. she's strapped.

550
00:29:27.365 --> 00:29:28.423
Oh. God. no.

551
00:29:31.369 --> 00:29:33.997
Mom. where is he?

552
00:29:59.397 --> 00:30:00.591
Maddie.

553
00:30:01.032 --> 00:30:02.090
Henry?

554
00:30:02.167 --> 00:30:04.727
Yeah. it's me. sweetheart. I'm
right here. I'm not going anywhere.

555
00:30:06.504 --> 00:30:08.734
All right. then
I won't. either.

556
00:30:09.274 --> 00:30:12.266
Besides. I don't really have
anything better to do right now.

557
00:30:13.144 --> 00:30:16.113
It's just a pen.
It's just a pen!

558
00:30:16.214 --> 00:30:19.149
What does this mean.
Mary? Tell us!

559
00:30:19.217 --> 00:30:22.186
I don't know. This feels more like
improvisation. This isn't his game.

560
00:30:22.253 --> 00:30:23.447
We got here in time.
Maybe we won.

561
00:30:23.521 --> 00:30:25.989
No. he's definitely going to kill
her dead. I just don't know how.

562
00:30:26.057 --> 00:30:27.922
He's been one step
ahead this whole time.

563
00:30:27.992 --> 00:30:29.050
Where's Shawn?

564
00:30:29.260 --> 00:30:30.784
Hopefully one step
ahead of us.

565
00:30:40.638 --> 00:30:41.798
Okay.

566
00:30:41.873 --> 00:30:45.070
All right. be honest with
me. You're surprised. right?

567
00:30:45.143 --> 00:30:47.668
I'm prettier than
you thought I'd be.

568
00:30:48.379 --> 00:30:50.313
It's the bone structure.

569
00:30:50.381 --> 00:30:53.908
I won. I beat you. That
was the deal. Let my mom go.

570
00:30:53.985 --> 00:30:56.579
You are just amazing.

571
00:30:56.654 --> 00:31:00.681
Just my most.
most admirable foe.

572
00:31:00.758 --> 00:31:03.784
But then. see. I knew you would
be. That's why I chose you.

573
00:31:03.862 --> 00:31:05.124
Because I'm...

574
00:31:05.196 --> 00:31:06.356
I'm your yin.

575
00:31:07.365 --> 00:31:09.265
Well. that's sweet.
Thank you for that.

576
00:31:09.334 --> 00:31:12.701
But you're completely
surrounded.

577
00:31:12.770 --> 00:31:14.203
There's no way
out of this for you.

578
00:31:20.745 --> 00:31:25.273
Hey. you know what I love about this
movie. Shawn? Its great resolution.

579
00:31:25.350 --> 00:31:26.908
Okay. so call me
old-fashioned.

580
00:31:26.985 --> 00:31:31.319
but really. is there anything more
satisfying than a solid ending?

581
00:31:31.389 --> 00:31:36.122
You call me a killer. but the
truth is. I complete things.

582
00:31:36.194 --> 00:31:40.631
And that is what people
really want. to feel complete.

583
00:31:40.698 --> 00:31:41.892
That. and
a corner booth.

584
00:31:45.003 --> 00:31:51.431
And now. our story. that we
created so beautifully together.

585
00:31:52.043 --> 00:31:53.169
is going to end.

586
00:31:53.878 --> 00:31:55.140
But how?

587
00:31:56.447 --> 00:31:58.608
Do you want to know
what it is?

588
00:31:58.683 --> 00:32:00.480
Or do you want
to be surprised?

589
00:32:04.055 --> 00:32:06.580
Let's dial up!
Move in slow.

590
00:32:09.594 --> 00:32:10.891
Stand down! Stand down!

591
00:32:12.063 --> 00:32:14.896
Stand down. Stand down.
Move them back. Let's go!

592
00:32:17.235 --> 00:32:21.604
Let me guess.
You want to die. right?

593
00:32:21.673 --> 00:32:23.504
That's the perfect
resolution?

594
00:32:23.574 --> 00:32:26.202
Gee. that's original.
You're a cliché.

595
00:32:27.178 --> 00:32:29.476
You're a knockoff
of a knockoff.

596
00:32:30.181 --> 00:32:32.809
I could have killed your
mom hours ago. Shawn.

597
00:32:32.884 --> 00:32:37.048
This switch has such a light
touch. like pinching a baby's cheek.

598
00:32:37.121 --> 00:32:39.612
And then. boom!
She blows up.

599
00:32:39.691 --> 00:32:41.283
How much fun would
that be to see?

600
00:32:41.359 --> 00:32:44.692
Oh. it gives me shivers.
I want to do that so badly!

601
00:32:44.762 --> 00:32:47.697
But then.
you wouldn't like me. Shawn.

602
00:32:47.765 --> 00:32:50.859
And I want you to like me.
Oh. God. I'm so torn.

603
00:32:51.569 --> 00:32:55.528
I need you to like me. because we're
going to be working together again.

604
00:32:55.606 --> 00:32:57.369
Oh. no. no. no. no.

605
00:32:57.442 --> 00:33:00.104
You're going to rot in a cell
with four padded walls. The end.

606
00:33:00.178 --> 00:33:02.339
No. The end
of the beginning.

607
00:33:03.214 --> 00:33:04.511
I'm going to write
a book.

608
00:33:04.582 --> 00:33:05.571
Our story.

609
00:33:06.150 --> 00:33:07.811
It's going to be epic.
A bestseller.

610
00:33:07.885 --> 00:33:10.319
And guess what? I want
you to write the forward.

611
00:33:10.388 --> 00:33:11.480
Pass.

612
00:33:12.457 --> 00:33:13.549
Okay.

613
00:33:15.193 --> 00:33:18.390
But think about it
on your date tonight.

614
00:33:35.780 --> 00:33:36.804
Clear!

615
00:33:36.881 --> 00:33:38.473
Take the subject!
Go! Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

616
00:33:38.549 --> 00:33:39.914
Go! Go! Go!

617
00:33:43.121 --> 00:33:44.383
Let's go.

618
00:33:47.025 --> 00:33:49.152
Okay.
All right. you're okay.

619
00:33:49.227 --> 00:33:51.092
You're okay. All right.

620
00:34:01.139 --> 00:34:04.302
<i>Think about it
on your date tonight.</i>

621
00:34:18.256 --> 00:34:21.248
She was there. Gus. she
was there the whole time.

622
00:34:21.325 --> 00:34:23.691
You got her. Shawn.
End of story.

623
00:34:25.363 --> 00:34:26.830
Congratulations.
Spencer.

624
00:34:26.898 --> 00:34:29.059
Don't be too excited
there. Mary.

625
00:34:29.133 --> 00:34:30.430
It's not like
we just apprehended

626
00:34:30.501 --> 00:34:32.560
Santa Barbara's most
notorious killer or anything.

627
00:34:32.637 --> 00:34:34.298
You're right. Gus. I'm sorry
to fly off the handle.

628
00:34:35.973 --> 00:34:40.205
I've spent the last 13 years
of my life with this person.

629
00:34:41.479 --> 00:34:43.106
I have to find a new hobby.

630
00:34:43.181 --> 00:34:44.341
Two words.

631
00:34:44.449 --> 00:34:45.473
Racquetball.

632
00:34:45.883 --> 00:34:46.872
That could work.

633
00:34:48.519 --> 00:34:50.714
Thanks for your help. man. I needed it.

634
00:34:51.522 --> 00:34:53.513
Gus. you play racquetball?
Goodbye. Mary.

635
00:34:57.662 --> 00:34:59.755
Until next time.
Okay. Okay.

636
00:35:04.702 --> 00:35:07.466
There we go.
Better?

637
00:35:11.375 --> 00:35:13.343
Henry. I told him
to go for it.

638
00:35:13.411 --> 00:35:15.140
That doesn't matter.

639
00:35:15.213 --> 00:35:17.807
What matters is that
you're both okay.

640
00:35:18.549 --> 00:35:22.280
You two are the most important
people in the world to me. you know.

641
00:35:22.353 --> 00:35:23.684
I do know.

642
00:35:29.427 --> 00:35:31.622
Mom! Let's get you
out of here.

643
00:35:31.696 --> 00:35:32.754
What do you need?
What can I do?

644
00:35:32.830 --> 00:35:35.424
Let's see. You already got me
kidnapped by a raging sociopath...

645
00:35:38.302 --> 00:35:39.997
Right. Check.
What else?

646
00:35:40.071 --> 00:35:41.902
Nothing! Nothing.
goose. I'm really fine.

647
00:35:41.973 --> 00:35:43.873
Your father's been taking
very good care of me.

648
00:35:43.941 --> 00:35:45.533
Well. be good.
Yep.

649
00:35:45.610 --> 00:35:48.602
If I'm not mistaken. you have
a very important date tonight.

650
00:35:48.679 --> 00:35:50.704
Oh. Mom. please.
I can reschedule.

651
00:35:50.781 --> 00:35:52.078
No. you won't!

652
00:35:53.184 --> 00:35:54.173
I'm fine!

653
00:35:54.719 --> 00:35:58.177
The crazy bitch snuck up from
behind me with chloroform.

654
00:36:01.192 --> 00:36:03.683
Life is more than
catching bad guys.

655
00:36:04.262 --> 00:36:06.628
You did a good
deed today.

656
00:36:06.697 --> 00:36:09.222
Now it's time
to go see about a girl.

657
00:36:12.503 --> 00:36:13.868
It's time to go see
about a...

658
00:36:15.940 --> 00:36:17.931
How you like
them apples?

659
00:36:21.279 --> 00:36:22.678
Well played. Mom.

660
00:36:23.447 --> 00:36:24.778
All right.

661
00:36:38.029 --> 00:36:39.018
Hey.

662
00:36:39.096 --> 00:36:42.065
Shawn. did you really
just catch Mr. Yang?

663
00:36:42.133 --> 00:36:44.499
Yes. I did. And he
turned out to be a she.

664
00:36:44.569 --> 00:36:46.366
Curious.
Yeah.

665
00:36:48.005 --> 00:36:50.997
Hey. I'm sorry I didn't
believe you earlier. I just. uh.

666
00:36:51.075 --> 00:36:52.064
really didn't.

667
00:36:53.044 --> 00:36:54.909
Half-apology
accepted.

668
00:36:54.979 --> 00:36:57.379
Uh. I cut a deal with
the theater manager.

669
00:36:57.448 --> 00:37:01.043
so this is still happening
in a big. big way.

670
00:37:01.852 --> 00:37:03.820
How do you feel
about popped corn?

671
00:37:03.888 --> 00:37:06.288
I like it.
I like it very much.

672
00:37:11.329 --> 00:37:12.921
Jules! What are you
doing here?

673
00:37:12.997 --> 00:37:15.090
What I mean is. you know.
who's going to fit Mr. Yang

674
00:37:15.166 --> 00:37:18.192
with her straightjacket
and iron mask with face grill?

675
00:37:18.269 --> 00:37:20.601
Something tells me there's
an entire precinct of officers

676
00:37:20.671 --> 00:37:22.195
bidding on that job
right now.

677
00:37:22.273 --> 00:37:25.936
Uh. can I interest you
in a Necco Wafer?

678
00:37:26.010 --> 00:37:28.604
Shawn. can you just not
talk for a few seconds?

679
00:37:28.679 --> 00:37:32.775
Look. I just wanted to tell
you that what you did today...

680
00:37:33.951 --> 00:37:37.512
I mean. I can't imagine being
able to function at that level

681
00:37:37.588 --> 00:37:39.783
while your mom
was... You know.

682
00:37:41.859 --> 00:37:46.796
I am. uh. clearly not as
good with words as you are.

683
00:37:46.864 --> 00:37:51.426
and I know that
things between us

684
00:37:51.502 --> 00:37:54.335
have been
a little complicated.

685
00:37:55.506 --> 00:37:59.670
and that there have probably been
some mixed signals. mostly from me.

686
00:37:59.744 --> 00:38:03.942
with regards to the time that we spend
together outside of the line of duty.

687
00:38:04.015 --> 00:38:05.039
Look. Jules...

688
00:38:05.116 --> 00:38:07.346
Shh! Please. just let me
finish stumbling through this.

689
00:38:07.418 --> 00:38:08.783
I'm almost done.
I promise.

690
00:38:10.154 --> 00:38:11.280
What I'm saying

691
00:38:12.456 --> 00:38:15.721
is that I think. maybe.
the best things.

692
00:38:16.694 --> 00:38:18.059
the richest things.

693
00:38:19.163 --> 00:38:20.994
aren't supposed
to come easily.

694
00:38:22.033 --> 00:38:24.194
and that sometimes the moments
that make the most sense

695
00:38:24.268 --> 00:38:27.999
happen when everything
else doesn't. and. well.

696
00:38:29.674 --> 00:38:32.666
I think you deserve more
than popcorn tonight.

697
00:38:37.181 --> 00:38:40.014
So why don't you let me
take you to dinner?

698
00:38:40.685 --> 00:38:43.347
Detective O'Hara. are you
asking me out on a date?

699
00:38:43.421 --> 00:38:44.547
I am.

700
00:38:45.256 --> 00:38:46.655
A proper one.

701
00:38:46.891 --> 00:38:47.983
Wow.

702
00:38:49.527 --> 00:38:51.757
I cannot believe this.

703
00:38:52.663 --> 00:38:54.096
All this time. and...

704
00:38:54.365 --> 00:38:56.765
Your timing
is just awful.

705
00:38:58.402 --> 00:39:00.393
It is?
Yeah. just dreadful.

706
00:39:01.372 --> 00:39:02.566
What?

707
00:39:02.640 --> 00:39:05.632
I can't go to dinner with you.
Jules. I'm already on a date.

708
00:39:05.710 --> 00:39:07.769
You are? What. here?

709
00:39:07.845 --> 00:39:09.472
Yeah. Right now.

710
00:39:09.747 --> 00:39:12.079
It's... It's weird. it's
a little weird. but. uh...

711
00:39:12.850 --> 00:39:13.839
Yeah.

712
00:39:15.019 --> 00:39:16.043
With Abigail.

713
00:39:16.120 --> 00:39:17.678
The one that got away.

714
00:39:17.755 --> 00:39:18.881
Yeah.

715
00:39:32.903 --> 00:39:34.393
Get out there.

716
00:39:36.741 --> 00:39:39.039
She's not going
to wait forever.

717
00:39:44.014 --> 00:39:45.106
Jules?

718
00:39:46.550 --> 00:39:50.919
I am so sorry
for snapping at you earlier.

719
00:39:51.155 --> 00:39:52.179
I know.

720
00:40:11.442 --> 00:40:12.466
You all right?

721
00:40:12.543 --> 00:40:15.068
Yeah. Why would you
even ask that?

722
00:40:15.146 --> 00:40:17.239
Mostly because you look like
you got punched in the stomach

723
00:40:17.314 --> 00:40:19.441
and stopped breathing
for a few seconds.

724
00:40:19.517 --> 00:40:22.452
Wow. I didn't realize
